    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **68 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n- **`AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2192 `AssignMemberId.java`** \u2014 now builds `memberId` as `REGION` + 2-digit fiscal year (from `registrationDate`) + `HASH8` (first-8-upper-hex of SHA-256 over normalized-telephone + lastName, unchanged) + a single Luhn `CHK` computed over the digits of `REGION+FY+HASH8`. Collision de-duplication now applies to the `memberId`. Verified output e.g. `NSW27198FE5293`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` renamed to `memberId`/`member_id`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings and their methods; `memberId` auto-maps from the entity; `locality` now derives the REGION from the `memberId` prefix (its leading letter run) instead of the customerCode; `fiscalYear` is unchanged and matches the FY embedded in `memberId`.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 both the human-readable line and the structured `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event now carry `memberId` as the owner's primary identifier (customerCode/membershipNumber gone).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the three fields with a single `memberId` schema (drives the generated `OwnerDto`); updated the `locality` description.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 `assignCode` step points at `AssignMemberId`; comments updated.\n- **DB schema (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) + hsqldb data.sql** \u2014 `customer_code` column renamed to `member_id`.\n\nAll the checkpoint tests that specify the new behaviour pass (Cp09/14/16/31 removals, Cp32/56 unified format, Cp41 collision, Cp48 fiscal year, Cp53 audit event, Cp17/29/42/55 region/segment), with no regressions across the full 68-test suite.",
